(a) The Nyquist rate is half the sampling frequency and the Nyquist interval is the inverse of the Nyquist rate.
- For Sa(200t), the frequency is 200 Hz, so the Nyquist rate is 200/pi Hz and the Nyquist interval is pi/200 s.
- For [Sa(200t)]^2, the frequency is 400 Hz, so the Nyquist rate is 400/pi Hz and the Nyquist interval is pi/400 s.


(b) The Nyquist rate is half the highest frequency component in the signal and the Nyquist interval is the inverse of the Nyquist rate.
- For Sa(200t), the highest frequency component is 200 Hz, so the Nyquist rate is 200/pi Hz and the Nyquist interval is pi/200 s.
- For [Sa(200t)]^2, the highest frequency components are 200 Hz and 400 Hz, so the Nyquist rate is the greater of these, which is 400/pi Hz, and the Nyquist interval is pi/400 s.
